\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Empirical evidence of hallucination phenomena in energy-carbon domain question answering. Comparative analysis reveals significant performance gaps between generic LLMs and domain-adapted models, with baseline models exhibiting factual inaccuracies and semantic incompleteness when handling specialized terminology and policy details. These systematic observations demonstrate the critical necessity of domain-specific adaptation for reliable energy-carbon applications.}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:overview}{{1}{3}{Empirical evidence of hallucination phenomena in energy-carbon domain question answering. Comparative analysis reveals significant performance gaps between generic LLMs and domain-adapted models, with baseline models exhibiting factual inaccuracies and semantic incompleteness when handling specialized terminology and policy details. These systematic observations demonstrate the critical necessity of domain-specific adaptation for reliable energy-carbon applications}{figure.1}{}}
\newlabel{fig:overview@cref}{{[figure][1][]1}{[1][3][]3}}
